I'm aiming for a 5V to 9V conversion, so I'll need to calculate the appropriate duty cycle.  I'll use the formula D = (Vout - Vin) / (Vout + Vin) to get a duty cycle of approximately 0.333.  This will help ensure the output voltage is correct.

I'll also check the inductor values to make sure they're suitable for the current levels.  For the SEPIC topology, I'll need to calculate the inductance values based on the input voltage, output voltage, and switching frequency.  I'll also ensure that the capacitors are large enough to filter out the ripple voltage.

